{"title":"2006 IMO Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine the least real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> such that the inequality \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/3/973b3ca7a4e5262cdd8bb6d67febe1dd03a72543.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left| ab(a^{2}-b^{2})+bc(b^{2}-c^{2})+ca(c^{2}-a^{2})\\right|\\leq M(a^{2}+b^{2}+c^{2})^{2}\\]\" width=\"465\" height=\"22\" /> \nholds for all real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9bdf3e496517e8f8742f81dd774be1f93cf6e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We claim that the least real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> satisfying the inequality is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/f/9af159bf92b0dc3755c46c2ac222b8474b589c7f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[M=\\frac{9\\sqrt{2}}{32}.\\]\" width=\"84\" height=\"41\" />\nLet\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/e/68ea33ba94fa24737bcf3a2fdddf5e0301ccfdfb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[E=ab(a^2-b^2)+bc(b^2-c^2)+ca(c^2-a^2).\\]\" width=\"341\" height=\"20\" />\nA direct factorization yields\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/1/ae1ca4a38fbe45db3e7f6546c1f9f8c198fb6f46.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[E=-(a+b+c)(a-b)(b-c)(c-a).\\]\" width=\"299\" height=\"18\" />\nBoth sides of the inequality are homogeneous of degree <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Hence, without loss of generality, we normalize\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/5/9d5523aaee42657bf099779eab4d23760baa29d0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2+b^2+c^2=1.\\]\" width=\"128\" height=\"17\" />\nThe problem then reduces to maximizing\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/7/e4730adf3efaa5508437961841e433294da729d6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|E|=|(a+b+c)(a-b)(b-c)(c-a)|\\]\" width=\"298\" height=\"18\" />\nunder this constraint.\n</p><p>Let\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b557a7c0d0ec324627cd6cd23538556c63116281.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[s=a+b+c,\\qquad p=ab+bc+ca,\\qquad q=abc,\\]\" width=\"375\" height=\"16\" />\nand set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/a/8cab5c27dc16fdfc4ab828cd7d6fb6d457406cd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t=s^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"17\" />. From the normalization,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/c/a1c4ad7506539ecc27f89c0b6bd6f5dbc485d793.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[p=\\frac{t-1}{2}.\\]\" width=\"79\" height=\"37\" />\nBy the Cauchy--Schwarz inequality,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/c/87cf518bab6156e70b1401409b7a067ec8e41710.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[s^2\\le 3(a^2+b^2+c^2)=3,\\]\" width=\"192\" height=\"20\" />\nso <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/5/cd542ed8a4c450533f55f55079325798beb75d88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t\\in[0,3]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Since\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/d/cadc752adef06012570f1f7034b8c02553997a6d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[E^2=(a+b+c)^2(a-b)^2(b-c)^2(c-a)^2=s^2\\Delta=t\\Delta,\\]\" width=\"424\" height=\"20\" />\nwhere\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/3/303957f36eebf2c55d98e56023eadbdd7c95c4b4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Delta=(a-b)^2(b-c)^2(c-a)^2,\\]\" width=\"225\" height=\"20\" />\nit suffices to maximize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/d/77daa7d7a0bd09db0bfe40b997390bcd9c44414f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t\\Delta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Viewing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> as the roots of the cubic\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/1/93188ee4752e2b95db990442aa8db859b71afecc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^3-sx^2+px-q=0,\\]\" width=\"176\" height=\"19\" />\nits discriminant is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/5/ae51a48262f552998af1f4ccf60fd7d737f47aee.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Delta=s^2p^2-4p^3-4s^3q+18spq-27q^2.\\]\" width=\"302\" height=\"19\" />\nFor fixed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> (hence fixed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" />), this is a quadratic polynomial in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> with negative leading coefficient <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/7/4d7dff96a26c5c196f016df7625dcb031d04051d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" />, and therefore concave. Its maximum is attained at the vertex, giving\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/c/a5cf51e2f0730479aecc080dbf78b776f6af042f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Delta_{\\max}=(s^2p^2-4p^3)+\\frac{(18sp-4s^3)^2}{108}.\\]\" width=\"293\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/7/ce759d94d7ea951de87f222e7da61aa33640fa0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s^2=t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/6/ad60dda3c53f4a41459a47d8ccc543e1b54f71bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=\\frac{t-1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"77\" height=\"38\" />, we compute\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/a/2ea3172e4ebb76fa9f88252cb94370f66c899627.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[s^2p^2-4p^3=\\frac{(t-1)^2(2-t)}{4},\\qquad (18sp-4s^3)^2=t(5t-9)^2.\\]\" width=\"468\" height=\"39\" />\nHence\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/c/eec0f407153448c3783bfb874fb332618e525a29.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Delta_{\\max}=\\frac{27(t-1)^2(2-t)+t(5t-9)^2}{108}.\\]\" width=\"299\" height=\"39\" />\nExpanding the numerator gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/3/3f352f646bb1843a47a362b26be10b857c29e183.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[27(-t^3+4t^2-5t+2)+(25t^3-90t^2+81t)=-2(t-3)^3,\\]\" width=\"455\" height=\"20\" />\nso\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/1/e01f8c2b7ba2889fd2c18b6e4f47c1ce1d6c6c54.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Delta_{\\max}=\\frac{(3-t)^3}{54}.\\]\" width=\"131\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Thus\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/f/5ff0f771de09480399a767657ecaad5085f8b42c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|E|^2\\le t\\Delta_{\\max}=\\frac{t(3-t)^3}{54}.\\]\" width=\"199\" height=\"39\" />\nDefine\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/1/cb17ce692de7f3ef0d654e6d39f8ca947f156f4f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(t)=\\frac{t(3-t)^3}{54},\\qquad t\\in[0,3].\\]\" width=\"235\" height=\"39\" />\nDifferentiating,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/5/ca5c6ee3ddfd872cf38924b2b28e578d13231eaa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f&#39;(t)=\\frac{(3-t)^2(3-4t)}{54},\\]\" width=\"188\" height=\"39\" />\nwhich vanishes at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/c/35c913cff7776ae19bed793a777bfc7157591527.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/1/851cf298db09e02b3cce1dabd77db105c42cce05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t=\\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"46\" height=\"38\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/3/eb376994e391c373ace49b7185b2111e6b410889.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(0)=f(3)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"128\" height=\"20\" />, the maximum occurs at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/1/851cf298db09e02b3cce1dabd77db105c42cce05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t=\\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"46\" height=\"38\" />, where\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/7/727221dcb1bc91a67f9105789c9d5284d1c0a910.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f\\!\\left(\\tfrac{3}{4}\\right)=\\frac{81}{512}.\\]\" width=\"96\" height=\"37\" />\nTherefore,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/f/29f449e1f0aea07e1c62b28ac6a2a042fe4da994.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|E|_{\\max}=\\sqrt{\\frac{81}{512}}=\\frac{9\\sqrt{2}}{32}.\\]\" width=\"186\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>At <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/1/851cf298db09e02b3cce1dabd77db105c42cce05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t=\\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"46\" height=\"38\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/f/15f018035a43b53609a904ec4e9a0251c17f1964.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=-\\frac{1}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"62\" height=\"38\" />, and the corresponding optimal value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/5/5a56237673d0d9be1aa9812dc617c247958fd64c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta_{\\max}&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"17\" />, ensuring the existence of three distinct real roots <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />. Hence equality is attainable (up to permutation and scaling), and the minimum is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/a/d2a6cc5d91992a3bd54d241c43f6dc088dceea34.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{M=\\frac{9\\sqrt{2}}{32}}.\\]\" width=\"96\" height=\"53\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO\" title=\"2006 IMO\">2006 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2006 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017171500\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.028 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.040 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 285/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9143/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.959      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.959      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:12692:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017171500 and revision id 276751. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}